Q: Error &quot;Trying to get property of non-object&quot; using -&gt;row-&gt;column_name after CodeIgniter&#39;s $this-&gt;db-&gt;get() A: <p>row() is a function and not a property.</p>

<pre><code>$id = $query-&gt;row()-&gt;id; 
</code></pre>

<p>or </p>

<pre><code>$id = $query-&gt;row(0)-&gt;id; 
</code></pre>

Q: Is it possible to specify corner radius as a percentage in an Android drawable? A: <p>If you define size (eg: 100dp x 100dp) to your shape, it means that your radius parameters are relative to the size. In this example radius will be %20</p>
<pre><code>&lt;?xml version=&quot;1.0&quot; encoding=&quot;utf-8&quot;?&gt;
&lt;shape xmlns:android=&quot;http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android&quot;&gt;
    &lt;size android:width=&quot;100dp&quot; android:height=&quot;100dp&quot; /&gt;    
    &lt;corners android:radius=&quot;20dp&quot; /&gt;
    &lt;solid android:color=&quot;#000000&quot; /&gt;
&lt;/shape&gt;
</code></pre>

Q: Recommendations for improving my structure A: <p>Just interpreting your code (notwithstanding any issues around genuine randomness) you could simplify as follows:</p>
<pre><code>from random import randrange
from socket import inet_aton

RANGES = (256, 256, 10, 10)

def rng_ipv4() -&gt; str:
    &quot;&quot;&quot;Generate IPv4 address with limitations&quot;&quot;&quot;
    return &quot;.&quot;.join(str(randrange(r)) for r in RANGES)

def firewall(ip_address: str) -&gt; bool:
    &quot;&quot;&quot;
    Validate ip address
    Must be valid in the context of the IPv4 specification and also custom limitations
    &quot;&quot;&quot;
    try:
        for p, r in zip(inet_aton(ip_address), RANGES):
            if p &gt;= r:
                break
        else:
            return True
    except OSError:
        pass
    return False

a = rng_ipv4()
print(a, firewall(a))
</code></pre>
